  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant in response to the cyclone disasters in Sri Lanka</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sri Lanka was struck by tropical cyclone Ditwah from 28 to 30 November 2025 resulting in mass displacement, severe flooding, landslips, power outages, and disruption to essential services. Landslide alerts remain active with red and amber warnings across central, western, and southern Sri Lanka. Prolonged rainfall has also resulted in high river levels, with significant flooding across many parts of the island.Through this project, IOM is ensuring that affected populations receive life-saving shelter and non-food item (NFI) assistance to meet their immediate needs, as well as strengthen the Shelter Cluster&#x2019;s coordination mechanisms to support unified standards, information management, and partner alignment for a coherent shelter response.</narrative>
  </description>
